            <ArticleTitle>[Local treatment in oligometastatic urological malignancies : evidence of wishful thinking ?]</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2083-2086</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the past, it was generally considered that the window of curability had been missed in metastatic solid cancers. At present, novel evidence suggests that oligometastatic cancer might be amenable to a multimodal curative treatment, including ablation of the primary tumour. In this article, we summarise the indications, the controversies and future perspectives of local treatment in oligometastatic urological malignancies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
